    "body": "Depends on: none. The repo currently reports bits/token in at least two accountings: the P2 certificate's 6.54 (WB metric) and the Gate C scorer's 11.88 — different metric families that will confuse the M.V.G. checkpoint. Pick one canonical definition (documented formula, nats→bits conversion, which distributions it covers), implement it in the Gate C harness and the certificate path, and annotate the historical values as their own families. Acceptance: one formula in GLOSSARY.md + all future reports cite it; BASELINE.md updated.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- One canonical bits/token definition (formula, nats→bits conversion, covered distributions) is documented in `docs/transformerless/GLOSSARY.md`.\n- The Gate C harness and the certificate path both emit the canonical metric; historical values are annotated as their own families.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The formula appears verbatim in GLOSSARY.md and is referenced by every subsequent report.\n- [ ] score_report.json and the certificate schema carry the canonical field name.\n- [ ] BASELINE.md marks 6.54 (P2 WB) and 11.88 (scorer) as their historical families with the mapping note.",
